# Code revision: 612f9c71

## Oracle finding

Pinned Java `ProcessQueue.containsMessage(null)` returns `false` before taking
its tree lock. Rust previously accepted only a non-null message reference. It
now exposes `contains_message_nullable(Option<&MessageExt>)`, which returns
false for `None` and forwards present messages to the existing lookup.

The invoked Java facade fixture records the null result, and the Rust facade
comparison uses the same case. Fixture SHA-256:
`edb43a544374bb1c5ae969bcdaa09ea3746a310b3d28dc86b459a18ecfcff551`.

## Commits

- `612f9c71 fix(consumer): match null ProcessQueue lookup`.
